      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, it’s nice to meet you. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S081",
      "patient_response": "Nice to meet you too. I'm here because... well, I just can't seem to keep myself together lately. \n\nEver since my daughter left for basic training, I feel like I come home to a dead house. It's really starting to affect my day-to-day life. I'm a sheet metal worker, and I find myself just sitting in the truck crying before my shifts. Once I'm actually on the floor, I'm missing steps on welding jobs I’ve done for years, and I've been snapping at the younger guys on the crew. \n\nEven when I'm off the clock, I've stopped going out on the water or working on my metal sculpture at home. I just... I just don’t see the point right now. I need some help getting back on track.",
